    <statement><p>Find an equation of a plane through the point (4, 5, -1)
which is orthogonal to the line 
<me>x = -5  - 1t, \quad y = 4
+ 2t, \quad  z = 5  - 4t</me> in which the coefficient of 
<m>x</m> is -1.</p>
<p>Equation: <fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1\mathopen{}\left(x-4\right)+2\mathopen{}\left(y-5\right)+\left(-4\right)\mathopen{}\left(z-\left(-1\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
